<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gijsbert Karel van Hogendorp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1762">1762</a>–<a href="/years/1834">1834</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gijsbert Karel van Hogendorp was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> statesman who led the provisional government of November 1813 that ended French rule and invited William Frederick of Orange to return as sovereign prince. He drafted the constitution of 1814 and served as foreign minister, later becoming a critic of royal economic policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gijsbert-karel-van-hogendorp.jpg" alt="Gijsbert Karel van Hogendorp" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean François Valois / After Cornelis Cels · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gijsbert_Karel_graaf_van_Hogendorp,_door_Jean_Francois_Valois_of_Cornelis_Cels.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
